      "story_id": 1,
      "headline": "Pakistan hosts US-Iran talks and launches intensive regional diplomacy as Munir leads Tehran mission and Shehbaz conducts Gulf-Turkey tour",
      "summary": "Pakistan emerged as the sole mediator in the US-Iran war, hosting a first round of direct talks in Islamabad (April 11) that ended without agreement, after which Field Marshal Asim Munir led a high-level delegation to Tehran (April 15-18) to deliver a US message and meet Iran's president, speaker, and foreign minister, while PM Shehbaz Sharif conducted a parallel four-day tour of Saudi Arabia, Qatar, and Turkey (April 15-18) to build regional consensus. The week ended with Trump announcing JD Vance, Witkoff, and Kushner would return to Islamabad for a second round, though Iran signaled reluctance citing 'excessive demands' and ceasefire breaches; Pakistan also Air Force-escorted Iranian negotiators home after the first round after Iran cited Israeli threat concerns.",
